From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emuTOS-MCD <darekadumon@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 21:06:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 157/184] The 20-second folder open was the DRV_INIT gate
 refusing a live drive

CDTEST's new per-op clocks caught it in one hardware run. The first
Getbpb of the session: 20,390 ms -- the init gate's 1200-frame budget
to the frame -- spent waiting for drive state $10/$20/$40 from a drive
reporting 1 and 6. The immediate retry ran the identical DRV_INIT
through the identical gate and succeeded in about two seconds. The
drive was ready; the gate refused the states it spins up through, and
the retry collected the credit. Warm numbers on the same run: Getbpb
25 ms, Dfree 150 ms, Fsfirst 5 ms, Fopen 5 ms -- once mounted, the
firmware path is already game-snappy. (Our fallback path measured
3,720 ms for the same Dfree; noted, not the priority.)

So the gate stops being able to fail the visit: on timeout, proceed to
the read. Every stage below has its own 200-frame bound and ROMREADN
snaps a willing drive to play, so proceeding costs seconds where
failing cost twenty. Budget down to 450 frames with the sting removed.
Doom never blocks on DRV_INIT at all; this is one step from that.
---
 bios/scdapi.h  |  2 +-
 bios/segacd2.S | 17 +++++++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/bios/scdapi.h b/bios/scdapi.h
index ee187bb..950240a 100644
--- a/bios/scdapi.h
+++ b/bios/scdapi.h
@@ -28,7 +28,7 @@
 #define SCDAPI_H
 
 #define SCD_COOKIE   0x53674344L        /* 'SgCD' */
-#define SCD_VERSION  25
+#define SCD_VERSION  26
 
 /* Everything the disc diagnostic prints, in one go. Taken in a single
  * call rather than twenty accessors so that the numbers in one report
diff --git a/bios/segacd2.S b/bios/segacd2.S
index b6f926d..d6f0521 100644
--- a/bios/segacd2.S
+++ b/bios/segacd2.S
@@ -249,7 +249,7 @@ _segacd_bios_lost:                      // mask bits seen switched off
         .globl  _segacd_bios_initwait
         .align  2
 _segacd_bios_initwait:                  // frames DRV_INIT may take
-        .long   1200
+        .long   450
 
 _segacd_bios_drvinit:                   // whether to wake with DRV_INIT
         // On, and that reverses a correction.
@@ -608,8 +608,21 @@ brd_wait_init:
         // the one the BIOS's own ROMREAD singles out as worth another
         // go, so "not finished yet" is the reading with the most behind
         // it. Whether it is right is what this change asks.
+        // On timeout, read anyway -- do not fail the visit.
+        //
+        // The hardware log that decided this: the first Getbpb of the
+        // session cost 20,390 ms, which is this gate's 1200-frame
+        // budget to the frame, spent waiting for state $10/$20/$40
+        // from a drive reporting 1 and 6 -- and the immediate retry
+        // re-ran the same DRV_INIT through the same gate and succeeded
+        // in about two seconds. The drive was ready; the gate refused
+        // the states it spins up through. Every stage below carries
+        // its own 200-frame bound, and ROMREADN itself snaps a willing
+        // drive to play, so proceeding costs at most seconds and
+        // failing here cost twenty. Doom never blocks on DRV_INIT at
+        // all: it retries per frame off CDBSTAT.
         cmp.l   _segacd_bios_initwait,d2
-        bcc     brd_fail_init
+        bcc     brd_awake
         move.w  #0x0081,d0              // CDB_STAT
         move.w  d0,50(a5)
         jsr     0x5F22
